.nh
.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-wallets-create - Create a wallet


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago wallets create [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint is used to create a wallet with prepaid credits.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--applies-to-billable-metric-codes\fP=""
	An array of billable metric codes to which the wallet is applicable. By specifying the billable metric codes in this field, you can restrict the wallet's usage to specific metrics only.

.PP
\fB--applies-to-fee-types\fP=""
	An array of fee types to which the wallet is applicable. By specifying the fee types in this field, you can restrict the wallet's usage to specific fee types only.

.PP
\fB--billing-entity-code\fP=""
	The code of the billing entity associated with the wallet. If not provided, the customer's billing entity is used.

.PP
\fB--code\fP=""
	The code of the wallet.

.PP
\fB--currency\fP=""
	The currency of the wallet.; one of: AED, AFN, ALL, AMD, ANG, AOA, ARS, AUD, AWG, AZN, BAM, BBD, BDT, BGN, BIF, BMD, BND, BOB, BRL, BSD, BWP, BYN, BZD, CAD, CDF, CHF, CLF, CLP, CNY, COP, CRC, CVE, CZK, DJF, DKK, DOP, DZD, EGP, ETB, EUR, FJD, FKP, GBP, GEL, GHS, GIP, GMD, GNF, GTQ, GYD, HKD, HNL, HRK, HTG, HUF, IDR, ILS, INR, ISK, JMD, JPY, KES, KGS, KHR, KMF, KRW, KYD, KZT, LAK, LBP, LKR, LRD, LSL, MAD, MDL, MGA, MKD, MMK, MNT, MOP, MRO, MUR, MVR, MWK, MXN, MYR, MZN, NAD, NGN, NIO, NOK, NPR, NZD, PAB, PEN, PGK, PHP, PKR, PLN, PYG, QAR, RON, RSD, RUB, RWF, SAR, SBD, SCR, SEK, SGD, SHP, SLL, SOS, SRD, STD, SZL, THB, TJS, TOP, TRY, TTD, TWD, TZS, UAH, UGX, USD, UYU, UZS, VND, VUV, WST, XAF, XCD, XOF, XPF, YER, ZAR, ZMW

.PP
\fB--expiration-at\fP=""
	The date and time that determines when the wallet will expire. It follows the ISO 8601 datetime format and is expressed in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).

.PP
\fB--external-customer-id\fP=""
	The customer external unique identifier (provided by your own application)

.PP
\fB--granted-credits\fP=""
	The number of free granted credits. Required only if there is no paid credits.

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--ignore-paid-top-up-limits-on-creation\fP=""
	If set to true, the wallet will ignore paid top-up limits on creation.

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--invoice-custom-section-invoice-custom-section-codes\fP=""
	List of unique codes identifying the invoice custom sections to apply. These override the default invoice custom sections configured at the customer or billing entity level.

.PP
\fB--invoice-custom-section-skip-invoice-custom-sections\fP=""
	Set to 'true' to exclude all invoice custom sections from PDF generation for invoices related to this resource. When 'true', 'invoice_custom_section_codes' is ignored.

.PP
\fB--invoice-requires-successful-payment\fP=""
	A boolean setting that, when set to true, delays issuing an invoice for a wallet top-up until a successful payment is made; if false, the invoice is issued immediately upon wallet top-up, regardless of the payment status. Default value of false.

.PP
\fB--metadata\fP=""
	Metadata to set as key-value pairs. Keys are strings (max 100 characters), values can be strings (max 255 characters) or null.

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	The name of the wallet.

.PP
\fB--paid-credits\fP=""
	The number of paid credits. Required only if there is no granted credits.

.PP
\fB--paid-top-up-max-amount-cents\fP=""
	Maximum amount of cents that can be top-up with a single paid transaction.

.PP
\fB--paid-top-up-min-amount-cents\fP=""
	Minimum amount of cents that can be top-up with a single paid transaction.

.PP
\fB--payment-method-payment-method-id\fP=""
	The unique identifier of the payment method (required when using a specific provider payment method).

.PP
\fB--payment-method-payment-method-type\fP=""
	The type of payment method to use.; one of: provider, manual

.PP
\fB--priority\fP=""
	Wallet priority for ordering when a customer has multiple wallets. Allowed values: 1-50, where 1 is highest priority and 50 is lowest. Defaults to 50.

.PP
\fB--purchase-order-number\fP=""
	The purchase order number associated with the wallet. It will be added to invoices generated for wallet top-ups, unless a more specific purchase order number is set on the wallet transaction or recurring transaction rule that triggered the top-up.

.PP
\fB--rate-amount\fP=""
	The rate of conversion between credits and the amount in the specified currency. It indicates the ratio or factor used to convert credits into the corresponding monetary value in the currency of the transaction.

.PP
\fB--recurring-transaction-rules\fP=""
	List of recurring transaction rules. Currently, we only allow one recurring rule per wallet.

.PP
\fB--transaction-metadata\fP=""
	This optional field allows you to store a list of key-value pairs that provide additional information or custom attributes. These key-value pairs will be included in the metadata of wallet transactions generated during the wallet creation process.

.PP
\fB--transaction-name\fP=""
	The name of the wallet transactions triggered when creating the wallet. It will appear on the invoice as the label for the fee. If not set, the label on the invoice will fallback to either 'Prepaid credits - {{wallet_name}}' if the wallet name is set, or 'Prepaid credits'.


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago wallets create --input @payload.json
  lago wallets create --input @payload.json --output json  # full resource
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlago-wallets(1)\fP
